#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:15
msgid "Test Hierarchy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:17
msgid ""
"PlatformIO looks for the tests in the project :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_test_dir`. The only folder with a name prefixed by "
"``test_`` is nominated for unit testing and should be an independent test/"
"application with its own ``main()`` function (``setup() / loop()`` for :ref:"
"`framework_arduino`, ``app_main()`` for :ref:`framework_espidf`). Nested "
"folders are supported and will help you to organize your tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:24
msgid ""
"The root :ref:`projectconf_pio_test_dir` and a folder of the active test are "
"automatically added to the ``CPPPATH`` scope (C Preprocessor Search Path). "
"Also, C/C++ files located in the root of :ref:`projectconf_pio_test_dir` "
"will be compiled together with the active test source files. The root :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_test_dir` is useful for placing configuration and extra C/C+"
"+ files related to the :ref:`unit_testing_frameworks`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:33
msgid ""
"If you have a single test application, you can place the source code files "
"directly in the :ref:`projectconf_pio_test_dir` folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:35
msgid ""
"If you want several test applications, you can organize them in subfolders "
"under :ref:`projectconf_pio_test_dir`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:38
msgid ""
"each test application goes into a subfolder with a name **starting** with "
"``test_``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:40
msgid ""
"additional levels of folders are allowed to properly organize your tests - "
"see the example **Pizza Project** below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:42
msgid ""
"the :ref:`projectconf_test_filter` option in :ref:`projectconf` or the :"
"option:`pio test --filter` option on the CLI will restrict the tests to only "
"those test suites whose path is relative to the :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_test_dir` and matches the filter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:46
msgid ""
"the :ref:`projectconf_test_ignore` option in :ref:`projectconf` or the :"
"option:`pio test --ignore` option on the CLI will ignore test suites whose "
"path is relative to the :ref:`projectconf_pio_test_dir` and matches the "
"filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:51
msgid ""
"Example of using the filter / ignore option in :ref:`projectconf` for the "
"**Pizza Project** below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:60
msgid ""
"will only execute the ``embedded/stove/test_humidity``, ``embedded/stove/"
"test_temperature`` test suites and will ignore the ``embedded/components/"
"sauce/test_tomatos`` test suite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:64
msgid "**Example of Pizza Project**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:66
msgid ""
"Let's demystify how PlatformIO handles unit tests using a virtual \"Pizza "
"Project\" having the following structure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:119
msgid ""
"The main source code (\"pizza baking\") is located in the ``src`` folder. "
"This is a production code. A cooking process consists of multiple "
"subprocesses and depends on the components located in the ``lib`` folder. "
"Each pizza's component can be tested independently using unit testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:124
msgid "The Pizza Project consists of 4 independent tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:126
msgid "``embedded/components/sauce/test_tomatos``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:127
msgid "``embedded/stove/test_humidity``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:128
msgid "``embedded/stove/test_temperature``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:129
msgid "``test_ingredients``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:131
msgid ""
"PlatformIO treats each test as an independent micro project with its own "
"source files and subfolders. You can include local header files using the "
"relative paths. For example, the ``test_ingredients/weighing.cpp`` source "
"file includes ``cheese.h`` as ``#include <include/cheese.h>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/structure/hierarchy.rst:136
msgid ""
"The ``unity_config.h`` and ``unity_config.cpp`` files are located in the "
"``embedded`` folder and are common for the ``embedded/components/sauce/"
"test_tomatos``, ``embedded/stove/test_humidity``, and ``embedded/stove/"
"test_temperature`` tests. This allows you to run a group of tests only on "
"the embedded target and route a test result output to the custom Serial/UART "
"interface. On the other hand, the ``test_ingredients`` test uses the default "
"Unity configuration provided by PlatformIO. For more details, please check "
"the documentation for the :ref:`unit_testing_frameworks_unity` testing "
"framework."
msgstr ""
